Chapter: SwarmKernel
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect

 A flow-field swarm, as a [Device] compute kernel. One GPU thread owns one
 particle. Each thread reads its particle's state (px, py, vx, vy) from an
 input buffer, steers its velocity toward a procedural flow field derived
 from position and time (fixed-point trig), integrates with inertia so the
 paths curve smoothly, wraps around the screen, and writes the new state to
 an output buffer. The host ping-pongs the two buffers each frame.

 This is emitter-tractable today: pure helpers plus one act-block kernel with
 buffer loads and stores, no per-neighbour loop. True neighbour-based boids
 (separation/alignment/cohesion) needs a bounded loop over the state buffer,
 which is recursion in Codex and requires recursion-to-loop lowering plus
 storage-pointer helper parameters in the WGSL plug -- the next emitter
 milestone.

 We say:

Section: Screen

  sw-width : Integer = 1024
  sw-height : Integer = 768
  sw-speed : Integer = 9

Section: Fixed-Point Trig

  sw-wrap : Integer -> Integer
  sw-wrap (a) = let m = a - (a / 6283) * 6283 in if m < 0 then m + 6283 else m

  sw-sin-core : Integer -> Integer
  sw-sin-core (x) =
    let x2 = x * x / 1000
    in let x3 = x2 * x / 1000
    in let x5 = x3 * x2 / 1000
    in x - x3 / 6 + x5 / 120

  sw-sin : Integer -> Integer
  sw-sin (raw) =
    let a = sw-wrap raw
    in if a <= 1570 then sw-sin-core a
    else if a <= 3141 then sw-sin-core (3141 - a)
    else if a <= 4712 then 0 - sw-sin-core (a - 3141)
    else 0 - sw-sin-core (6283 - a)

  sw-cos : Integer -> Integer
  sw-cos (raw) = sw-sin (raw + 1570)

Section: Flow Field

 The flow angle at a point cycles across space and drifts with time, giving
 a few large vortices that evolve. cos/sin of the angle give the target
 velocity direction; sw-speed scales the magnitude.

  sw-flow-ang : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sw-flow-ang (px) (py) (frame) =
    sw-wrap ((sw-sin (px * 5 + frame * 4) + sw-sin (py * 5 - frame * 3)) * 3 + frame * 2)

  sw-flow-vx : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sw-flow-vx (px) (py) (frame) = sw-cos (sw-flow-ang px py frame) * sw-speed / 1000

  sw-flow-vy : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sw-flow-vy (px) (py) (frame) = sw-sin (sw-flow-ang px py frame) * sw-speed / 1000

 Inertia: ease the velocity toward the flow so paths curve instead of
 snapping. Positions wrap toroidally.

  sw-new-vx : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sw-new-vx (px) (py) (vx) (frame) = (vx * 7 + sw-flow-vx px py frame) / 8

  sw-new-vy : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sw-new-vy (px) (py) (vy) (frame) = (vy * 7 + sw-flow-vy px py frame) / 8

  sw-wrap-pos : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sw-wrap-pos (v) (m) = let r = v - (v / m) * m in if r < 0 then r + m else r

  sw-new-px : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sw-new-px (px) (py) (vx) (frame) = sw-wrap-pos (px + sw-new-vx px py vx frame) sw-width

  sw-new-py : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sw-new-py (px) (py) (vy) (frame) = sw-wrap-pos (py + sw-new-vy px py vy frame) sw-height

Section: Swarm Kernel

 One thread per particle. Read state from inb, write advanced state to outb.

  swarm-step : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  swarm-step (inb) (outb) (frame) (gid) = act
    px <- device-load inb (gid * 4)
    py <- device-load inb (gid * 4 + 1)
    vx <- device-load inb (gid * 4 + 2)
    vy <- device-load inb (gid * 4 + 3)
    s0 <- device-store outb (gid * 4) (sw-new-px px py vx frame)
    s1 <- device-store outb (gid * 4 + 1) (sw-new-py px py vy frame)
    s2 <- device-store outb (gid * 4 + 2) (sw-new-vx px py vx frame)
    device-store outb (gid * 4 + 3) (sw-new-vy px py vy frame)
  end
